{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1354901-doubts-about-materials-and-licenses","id":1354901,"title":"Doubts about Materials and Licenses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-14T10:27:54-08:00","id":1354901,"title":"Doubts about Materials and Licenses","content":"People, one (probably big and complicated) question. The Storyteller System, in his five incarnations, Storytelling, in his two, or Storypath are under any sort of Dnd OGL-like License to create contente? I am not familiar with the Storytellers Vault rules and would like to know if anyone would be allowed to create a game using the rules of one of the systems and market it in any way even outside the Vault. And if it could even be used as the bases for a fanmade video game.<br /> <br /> Sorry for any grammar mistake, english is not my first language.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13198-mateusdragon","name":"mateusdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T11:21:38-08:00","id":1354904,"title":"","content":"To my knowledge, no you cannot. The Storyteller\u2019s Vault and Storypath Nexus only allow supplements for existing games, not entirely new properties. The systems themselves are owned by White Wolf and Onyx Path respectively and can only be used with their permission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T07:33:41-08:00","id":1355631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1354901-doubts-about-materials-and-licenses?p=1354904#post1354904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my knowledge, no you cannot. The Storyteller\u2019s Vault and Storypath Nexus only allow supplements for existing games, not entirely new properties. The systems themselves are owned by White Wolf and Onyx Path respectively and can only be used with their permission.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know game mechanics cannot be copyrighted on their own, but the specific terms and the way they are used can be legally protected in combination with the mechanics, so if you change the terminology there is no problem.<br /> <br /> The OGL was needed to allow people to make content for D&amp;D, but Pathfinder would have been possible without the OGL, for instance. The OGL simply got Paizo in the habit of making D20 products.<br /> <br /> It's risky because you have to make sure your explanation of the rules and how they're presented is not too close to the &quot;original&quot; but apart from that nobody can stop you from using the same rules.<br /> <br /> However, even if you're in the right, you can still get sued, and even if that's a lawsuit you would win if your expression of the rules is sufficiently unique, it's still a legal battle you'd first have to fight with a company, which you may not have the means to do.<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: people on a forum are <i>not</i> a good source of legal advice!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 12-18-2019, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]}